# conf/fleet-env-internal.list — FLEET_* names the scripts read that are NOT
# settings (issue #1101). bin/conf-surface-selftest.sh holds bin/ to: every
# ${FLEET_X:-…} a script reads is either a key in fleet.conf.example (any @tier,
# including internal) or listed here — so an undocumented knob cannot quietly
# join the config surface again. One name per line, then its kind and a reason:
#   handoff  env one fleet process sets for another (never in a conf)
#   seam     a test-injection point (fake command, fixed clock, sandbox path)
#   path     a state/log/cache location override
#   knob     a hand-override tuning value with a safe in-code default
#   alias    a retired twin of a documented key, still read for old confs
#   legacy / doc  see the reason
# Adding a line here is a decision: a knob an operator would plausibly change
# belongs in fleet.conf.example (with a tag line) instead.

FLEET_ACCOUNT_LABEL                handoff: the Claude account label a launch was assigned
FLEET_ACCOUNT_PHASE_WINDOW         knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (fleet-account.sh)
FLEET_ACCOUNT_SELECTED             handoff: the account pick already ran for this launch
FLEET_ACCOUNT_TARGET               handoff: the account a migrate/move relaunches on
FLEET_ALERTS_ALLCAPPED_SECS        knob: how long an `accounts · all capped` stamp stays an alert (fleet-alerts.sh, 900)
FLEET_ALERTS_EVENT_DEDUP           knob: same kind + text within this many seconds is one alerts event (fleet-alerts.sh event, 60)
FLEET_ALERTS_EVENT_KEEP            knob: how long alerts.events keeps a background event (fleet-alerts.sh, 2592000 = 30 days)
FLEET_ALERTS_EVENT_LIVE            knob: how long a background event counts as a ▲ row before it is popup history (fleet-alerts.sh, 3600)
FLEET_ALERTS_HISTORY_ROWS          knob: how many past events the alerts popup lists (fleet-alerts.sh, 100)
FLEET_ALERTS_HUB_FLASH_SECS        knob: hub unreachable this long before the one hub-lost flash (fleet-alerts.sh, 300)
FLEET_ALERTS_DISK                  seam: 0 skips the alerts producer's own df (a selftest that counts df calls)
FLEET_ALERTS_LOAD_PCT              knob: load per core ×100 at which `machine · load high` is raised (fleet-alerts.sh, 80, #1616)
FLEET_ALERTS_MACHINE               knob: 0 turns off the machine load / memory alerts (fleet-alerts.sh, #1616; selftests set it)
FLEET_ALERTS_MEM_PCT               knob: used-memory % at which `machine · memory high` is raised (fleet-alerts.sh, 85, #1616)
FLEET_ALERTS_MUTE_SECS             knob: how long `m` in the alerts popup mutes a row (fleet-alerts.sh, 3600)
FLEET_ALERTS_STALL_TTL             knob: how long a forgotten `stalled` alert outlives its killed waiter (fleet-alerts.sh, 21600)
FLEET_ALERTS_TRACE                 knob: how long a cleared alert keeps its ↻ row (fleet-alerts.sh, 1800)
FLEET_ALERTS_TTL                   knob: status-bar refresh interval of alerts.ndjson (fleet-alerts.sh, 5; 0 = every render)
FLEET_ANSWER_POLL                  knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (fleet-answer.sh)
FLEET_ANSWER_TIMEOUT               knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (fleet-answer.sh)
FLEET_AWAIT_ARMED                  handoff: fleet-await re-exec guard (alarm armed once)
FLEET_AWAIT_CPU_PCT                knob: % of a core above which a `working` child counts as busy, not stalled (fleet-await.sh, 10)
FLEET_AWAIT_TICK                   knob: seconds between ledger-file checks while waiting; a change reads at once (fleet-await.sh, 1, #1272)
FLEET_BASE_DEPS_LOG                path: state/log location override (fleet-deps-link.sh)
FLEET_BASE_DEPS_RETRY_BASE         knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (fleet-deps-link.sh)
FLEET_BASE_DEPS_RETRY_CAP          knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (fleet-deps-link.sh)
FLEET_BASE_SYNC                    knob: per-repo 0 opts a repo out of base-branch sync
FLEET_BASE_SYNC_LEASE_TTL          knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (fleet-base-sync.sh)
FLEET_BG_SOCK                      handoff: the background peer socket a message is sent over
FLEET_BOOTSTRAP_GIT_BASE           seam: an injectable command/path for tests (fleet-login-bootstrap.sh)
FLEET_BOOT_ID_CMD                  seam: a fake boot-session id for the diskguard crash harvest (fleet-diskguard.sh, #1294)
FLEET_C                            path: the dash cache root ($TMPDIR/.claude-dash) — tests point it at a sandbox
FLEET_CC_PROJECTS_DIR              path: state/log location override (fleet-migrate.sh)
FLEET_CC_SESSIONS_DIR              path: state/log location override (fleet-lib.sh)
FLEET_CLAUDE_COMM                  seam: the process name pane scans treat as Claude
FLEET_CLAUDE_INSTALL_CMD           seam: the Claude Code installer command (fleet-login-bootstrap.sh) — tests swap in a stub
FLEET_CLAUDE_TMP_ROOT              seam: the Claude scratchpad root the listener sweep anchors on (selftest sandbox)
FLEET_CLEANUP_LEASE_TTL            knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (fleet-cleanup-daemon.sh)
FLEET_CODEX_ACCOUNT                handoff: the codex account a launch was assigned
FLEET_CODEX_MANAGED                handoff: marks a codex launch as fleet-managed
FLEET_CODEX_PROFILE                handoff: an explicit codex profile for this launch
FLEET_COLLECT_QUOTAWATCH           knob: auto|never — whether the collector runs the quotawatch phase inline
FLEET_COMPACT_SEND_GRACE           knob: seconds fleet-compact-send.sh waits for the Stop hook to return before its idle check (2)
FLEET_COMPACT_RESUME_GRACE         knob: seconds fleet-compact-resume.sh waits after the restore before its idle check (3)
FLEET_COMPACT_RESUME_TIMEOUT       knob: how long fleet-compact-resume.sh holds for an untyped-at pane before giving up (90)
FLEET_COMPACT_RESUME_WATCH         knob: how long fleet-compact-resume.sh watches a stale `working` for the pane to settle before skip:stale (600, #1572)
FLEET_COMPACT_SEND_TIMEOUT         knob: how long fleet-compact-send.sh holds for an idle, untyped-at pane before giving up (90)
FLEET_CONFIG_SHOW_INTERNAL         knob: fcfg_table lists @tier=internal rows too (#1101) — a per-call switch, not a conf setting
FLEET_CONTEXT_LIMIT                alias: retired twin of FLEET_CTX_WINDOW (#1101) — still read, wins when set
FLEET_CRASH_JOURNAL_CMD            seam: a fake previous-boot kernel journal for the Linux crash harvest (fleet-diskguard.sh)
FLEET_CRASH_REPORT_DIR             path: where the system writes panic/Jetsam reports (fleet-diskguard.sh, /Library/Logs/DiagnosticReports)
FLEET_DAEMON_IDLE_PROBE_BUDGET     knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (fleet-daemon-lib.sh)
FLEET_DAEMON_ROOT                  path: state/log location override (fleet-daemon-lib.sh)
FLEET_DAEMON_WEDGED_MULT           knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (fleet-daemon-lib.sh)
FLEET_DASH_LAUNCHER                seam: an injectable command/path for tests (fleet-ui-refresh.sh)
FLEET_DASH_MANUAL_SUB_BIN           seam: fake manual quota gate for picker tests (dash-migrate.sh)
FLEET_DASH_MIGRATE_BIN             seam: an injectable command/path for tests (dash-migrate.sh)
FLEET_DASH_TOAST                   handoff: dash-migrate.sh `to` run from a confirm-before also shows its refusal (#1620)
FLEET_DASH_POPUP_MAX_AGE           knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (dash-popup-wait.sh)
FLEET_DASH_POPUP_POLL              knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (dash-popup-wait.sh)
FLEET_DELIVERY_SIG                 handoff: the webhook delivery signature the bridge verifies
FLEET_DEPLOY_PROBE_MAX             knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (tmux-pr-refresh.sh)
FLEET_DEPLOY_TTL                   knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (tmux-pr-refresh.sh)
FLEET_DEPLOY_TTL_FAILED            knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (tmux-pr-refresh.sh)
FLEET_DEPS_LOGIN_SHELL             seam: the login shell the deps probe asks for PATH (fleet-deps-link.sh)
FLEET_DEPS_NOW                     seam: a fixed clock for the deps retry backoff
FLEET_DEPS_TOOL_DIRS               seam: extra node/tool dirs the deps linker searches (fleet-deps-link.sh)
FLEET_DISKGUARD_SOURCE             seam: source fleet-diskguard.sh as a library without running it
FLEET_DISK_COOLDOWN                knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (fleet-diskguard.sh)
FLEET_DISK_TARGET                  path: the volume diskguard measures (default $TMPDIR)
FLEET_DISPATCH_LEASE_DIR           path: state/log location override (fleet-cleanup-daemon.sh)
FLEET_DISPATCH_LEASE_TTL           knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (fleet-dispatch.sh)
FLEET_EMIT_DIR                     path: state/log location override (fleet-emit.sh)
FLEET_EMIT_QUEUE_MAX               knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (fleet-emit.sh)
FLEET_EMIT_TIMEOUT                 knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (fleet-emit.sh)
FLEET_EPIC_BACKSTOP_BUSY_CMD       seam: a fake "is the box busy" probe for the EPIC backstop
FLEET_EPIC_BACKSTOP_FIND_CMD       seam: a fake local window lookup for the EPIC backstop (#1110)
FLEET_EPIC_RUNNING_TTL             knob: how long the epic-running heartbeat stays fresh (2700 s, fleet-epic-heartbeat.sh / fleet_epic_running, #953)
FLEET_FILES_PROBE_CMD              seam: a fake open-file-table reading for fleet_files_probe ("<used> <max>")
FLEET_FOLD_POLL                    knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (fleet-repo.sh)
FLEET_FOLD_WAIT                    knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (fleet-repo.sh)
FLEET_FSEVENTSD_WARN_CPU           knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (fleet-diskguard.sh)
FLEET_FZF_FOOTER                   handoff: 1/0, whether fzf takes --footer — probed once, inherited by a popup (fleet-popup-lib.sh, #1619)
FLEET_HANDOFF_COPY_LINES           knob: issue-body lines a handoff may copy before `check` hints (fleet-handoff-file.sh, 5; 0 = off)
FLEET_HANDOFF_DIR                  path: state/log location override (fleet-handoff-file.sh)
FLEET_HANDOFF_HARD_TIMEOUT         knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (fleet-handoff-cycle.sh)
FLEET_HANDOFF_LOG_DIR              path: state/log location override (fleet-handoff-cycle.sh)
FLEET_HANDOFF_MANIFEST             handoff: the handoff manifest a relaunch resumes from
FLEET_HANDOFF_MARGIN_MIN           knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (fleet-handoff-invariant.sh)
FLEET_HANDOFF_PICKUP_CMD           seam: an injectable command/path for tests (fleet-handoff-cycle.sh)
FLEET_HANDOFF_POLL                 knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (fleet-handoff-cycle.sh)
FLEET_HANDOFF_RETRY_AFTER          knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (fleet-handoff-cycle.sh)
FLEET_HANDOFF_VERIFY_TIMEOUT       knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (fleet-handoff-cycle.sh)
FLEET_HEAVY_BIN                    seam: the fleet-heavy.sh path bash-guard.py prefixes (fleet-heavy-selftest.sh)
FLEET_HEAVY_DIR                    path: the machine-wide heavy-slot dir (default /Users/Shared/claude-fleet/heavy)
FLEET_HUB_RECEIPT_WAIT             knob: seconds a cross-machine send waits for the hub's delivery receipt before saying queued (fleet-report-parent.sh / fleet-peer-send.sh, 4, #1647)
FLEET_MACHINE_SESSIONS_DIR         path: the machine-wide per-login session-count dir (default /Users/Shared/claude-fleet/sessions)
FLEET_HEAVY_HELD                   handoff: fleet-heavy.sh sets it for its child so nested heavies pass through
FLEET_HISTORY_LEDGER               path: state/log location override (fleet-history.sh)
FLEET_HOST_TUNE_MAXFILES_PLIST     seam: the maxfiles LaunchDaemon plist path (fleet-host-tune.sh)
FLEET_HUB                          handoff: marks the hub pane (operator seat), set at hub spawn
FLEET_HOME_TRACE                   knob: 0 switches the ⌂ latency trace off (fleet-trace-lib.sh, #1611)
FLEET_HOME_MS                      handoff: the ⌂ latency trace's marks, hub-zoom.sh → the picker inside the popup (fleet-trace-lib.sh, #1611)
FLEET_HUB_VISITS_LOGDIR            path: state/log location override (fleet-hub-visits.sh)
FLEET_HUB_VISITS_MAX               knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (fleet-hub-visits.sh)
FLEET_INSTALL_BIN                  path: where `curl <hub>/install | sh` (fleet-install.sh) puts the fleet client — ~/.local/bin by default; the installer runs before any fleet.conf exists (#1470)
FLEET_INSTALL_BREW_PREFIX          seam: brew prefix substituted into plists (fleet-install-apply.sh)
FLEET_INSTALL_CLAUDE               seam: an injectable command/path for tests (fleet-install-apply.sh)
FLEET_INSTALL_DAEMON_DIR           path: system LaunchDaemons dir override (fleet-install-apply.sh)
FLEET_INSTALL_LAUNCHCTL            seam: an injectable command/path for tests (fleet-install-apply.sh)
FLEET_INSTALL_LOGIN                seam: the login whose system LaunchDaemons are rendered (fleet-install-apply.sh)
FLEET_INSTALL_HOME                 seam: the __HOME__ a daemon template renders to — another login's when rendering for it (fleet-install-apply.sh --render-system, #1192)
FLEET_INSTALL_PLATFORM             seam: launchd|systemd|none instead of uname (fleet-install-apply.sh)
FLEET_INSTALL_NO_DEPS              seam: 1 = fleet-install.sh --no-deps — skip the tmux step (fleet-install-selftest.sh legs B-E; #1629)
FLEET_INSTALL_NO_RUN               seam: 1 stops fleet-install.sh from exec'ing `fleet` at the end (fleet-install-selftest.sh pipes the installer)
FLEET_INSTALL_RC                   seam: the rc file fleet-install.sh appends its PATH line to, instead of the one $SHELL implies (fleet-install-selftest.sh)
FLEET_INSTALL_ROOT                 path: the install to apply to (fleet-install-apply.sh)
FLEET_INSTALL_SUDO                 seam: the sudo prefix for system LaunchDaemons (fleet-install-apply.sh), and for the tmux step of fleet-install.sh (#1629)
FLEET_INSTALL_SYSTEMCTL            seam: an injectable command/path for tests (fleet-install-apply.sh)
FLEET_ISSUES_REFRESH_CMD           seam: an injectable command/path for tests (fleet-webhook.sh)
FLEET_ISSUE_BRIDGE_STATE_DIR       path: state/log location override (fleet-issue-bridge.sh)
FLEET_LAND_LEASE_DIR               path: state/log location override (fleet-base-sync.sh)
FLEET_LANG_RULE_RESUME             handoff: the one-language rule text injected into a resume
FLEET_LANG_RULE_SEED               handoff: the one-language rule text injected into a seed
FLEET_LATCH_RESET_SOURCE           seam: source the latch-reset hook as a library without running it
FLEET_LAUNCHD_AGENTS_DIR           path: state/log location override (fleet-daemon-watch.sh)
FLEET_LAUNCH_SESSION               handoff: the fleet session a launch is for (pool adapter check)
FLEET_MANUAL_ACCOUNT_BIN           seam: fake fresh quota reader for manual target tests (fleet-manual-sub.sh)
FLEET_LADDER_LOG_MAX_BYTES         knob: size cap for context-ladder.log + handoff-cycle.log, cut to the newest rows filling half the cap (1 MiB; 0 = no cap)
FLEET_LEDGER_WATCH                 knob: 0 turns the ledger-watch daemon into a no-op
FLEET_LEDGER_WATCH_LEASE_TTL       knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (fleet-ledger-watch.sh)
FLEET_LIVE_DIR                     path: the live install checkout (default ~/.claude/fleet) — fleet-install-version.sh, fleet-doctor.sh, and the hub refresh loop's stable mark (its local refs/tags/stable judges every machine's version, #644)
FLEET_LIVE_ROOT                    path: state/log location override (fleet-daemon-lib.sh)
FLEET_LOGIN_HOMES                  seam: an injectable command/path for tests (fleet-login-new.sh)
FLEET_LOOP_AGENT                   handoff: which agent the /loop spec belongs to
FLEET_LOOP_SPEC                    handoff: the /loop spec a relaunched agent restores
FLEET_CLAUDE_RSS_EVERY             knob: min seconds between memguard fat-session checks (fleet-memguard.sh, 30)
FLEET_MEM_INTERVAL                 knob: seconds between memguard samples (fleet-memguard.sh, 2)
FLEET_MEM_KILLED_TTL               knob: how long the dash keeps a window's @mem_killed badge (fleet-memguard.sh, 3600)
FLEET_MEM_MAX_TICKS                seam: stop the memguard loop after N samples (the selftest drives the ring with it)
FLEET_MEM_ORPHAN_EVERY             knob: min seconds between memguard orphan sweeps (fleet-memguard.sh, 60)
FLEET_MEM_PROBE_CMD                seam: a fake memory-pressure reading for fleet_mem_probe ("<level> <avail%> <compressor%> <swapMB>")
FLEET_MEM_PS_CMD                   seam: a fake process table for fleet_proc_mem_rows
FLEET_LOAD_PROBE_CMD               seam: a fake 1-min load-per-core reading for _fleet_load_per_core (machine admission, #1090)
FLEET_MEM_TOTAL_MB                 seam: a fixed physical-memory figure for fleet_mem_total_mb
FLEET_METRICS                      knob: 0 = no machine-metrics rows from diskguard/memguard (#1294, 1)
FLEET_METRICS_KEEP_DAYS            knob: machine/metrics-*.tsv retention in days (fleet-lib.sh, 7)
FLEET_MIGRATE_BOOT_WAIT            knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (fleet-migrate.sh)
FLEET_MIGRATE_CLOSE_WAIT           knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (fleet-migrate.sh)
FLEET_MIGRATE_DETACHED             handoff: marks the --force-self re-exec so it skips the own-window refusal (fleet-migrate.sh, #1474)
FLEET_MIGRATE_EXIT_WAIT            knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (fleet-migrate.sh)
FLEET_MIGRATE_FAILOVER_PY          seam: an injectable command/path for tests (fleet-migrate.sh)
FLEET_MIGRATE_LAUNCH               seam: an injectable command/path for tests (fleet-migrate.sh)
FLEET_MIGRATE_SELF_IDLE_WAIT       knob: how long a --force-self move waits for the caller's turn to end (fleet-migrate.sh, 1800)
FLEET_MOVE_CMD                     seam: the fleet-move.sh fleet-spot-evacuate.sh runs per fleet (default this bin's; #1428)
FLEET_OFFBOARD_ARCHIVE_DIR         path: offboarding home-archive dir override; --archive-dir is the CLI form (fleet-login-remove.sh)
FLEET_MIGRATION_LOCKED             handoff: a transition lock the caller already holds
FLEET_MOD_ALIVE_SECS               knob: a mod heartbeat younger than this is alive (fleet_mod_alive, fleet-doctor.sh; 45 = three missed beats)
FLEET_MOD_DONE_SECS                knob: how long fleet_session_command waits for the mod to finish a taken command before answering 6 (running)
FLEET_MOD_TAKE_SECS                knob: how long fleet_session_command waits for the mod to take a post before cancelling it (exit 4)
FLEET_MODEL_SWITCH_DIALOG          knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (fleet-model-switch.sh)
FLEET_MODEL_SWITCH_SCROLL          knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (fleet-model-switch.sh)
FLEET_MODEL_SWITCH_TRACE           knob: debug trace for the model switch
FLEET_MODEL_SWITCH_VERIFY          knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (fleet-model-switch.sh)
FLEET_MOVE_BOOT_WAIT               knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (fleet-move-remote.sh)
FLEET_MOVE_CLOSE_WAIT              knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (fleet-move.sh)
FLEET_MOVE_EXIT_WAIT               knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (fleet-move.sh)
FLEET_MOVE_LAUNCH                  seam: an injectable command/path for tests (fleet-move-remote.sh)
FLEET_MOVE_REBALANCE_MAX           knob: most sessions one `fleet-move.sh --rebalance` moves, default 2 (#1426)
FLEET_MOVE_TERM_WAIT               knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (fleet-move.sh)
FLEET_NEEDS_PLAIN_SECS             knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (tmux-spinner.sh)
FLEET_NEEDS_RECONCILE_SECS         knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (tmux-spinner.sh)
FLEET_NEEDS_STRIKE_TTL             knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (tmux-spinner.sh)
FLEET_NEEDS_TRACE                  knob: debug trace for the needs-reconcile spinner
FLEET_ORIGIN_GATE                  seam: 0 skips the spawn's live-parent gate (fleet_origin_gate, issue #1355) — tests whose parent key has no window
FLEET_PEER_MODE                    handoff: the sender's permission mode stamped on a cross-session message
FLEET_PEER_QUEUE_TTL               knob: seconds a queued report/message waits for its recipient before EXPIRED (fleet-peer-queue.sh, 604800 = the hub relay TTL, #1647)
FLEET_PICK_MODEL                   handoff: the model an account pick is evaluated for
FLEET_PLUGIN_NAME                  knob: the Claude plugin namespace fleet commands resolve under
FLEET_POOL_PROBE_TIMEOUT           knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (scratch-pool.sh)
