FLEET_REFOCUS_SOURCE               seam: the SessionStart source refocus-hook.sh acts on, instead of stdin
FLEET_REFUSE_MS                    knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (dash-issue-session.sh)
FLEET_REPORT_FROM                  handoff: the from-name a child report is sent under
FLEET_REPOS                        legacy: pre-#788 cache pin list, superseded by repos/ overlays; kept as the collector selftests' repo seam
FLEET_RESTORE_DIALOG_RE            knob: ERE for a dialog awaiting a human after resume (fleet-restore.sh outcome probe, #1265)
FLEET_RESTORE_NOCONV_RE            knob: ERE for a refused resume ("No conversation found") (fleet-restore.sh, #1265)
FLEET_RESTORE_LOG                  path: state/log location override (fleet-restore.sh)
FLEET_RESTORE_PROBE_SECS           knob: how long restore watches a resumed window for its outcome (fleet-restore.sh, 5)
FLEET_RESTORE_PROMPT_RE            knob: ERE for the agent input prompt = resumed (fleet-restore.sh, #1265)
FLEET_RESTORE_REJECT_ALARM         knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (fleet-restore.sh)
FLEET_RESTORE_SESS                 handoff: the session a restore targets
FLEET_RESTORE_STALE_MAP_AGE        knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (fleet-restore.sh)
FLEET_RESTORE_TMP_MAX_MIN          knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (fleet-restore.sh)
FLEET_SEED_REPO                    knob: the starter repo a new login's first-login bootstrap brings its fleet up on; read before any conf exists (fleet-login-bootstrap.sh)
FLEET_SESSION                      handoff: the fleet session a pane/popup belongs to, exported by the spawner
FLEET_SESSION_END_REASON           handoff: why the SessionEnd hook fired (set by the stopper)
FLEET_SIDEBAR_CURRENT              handoff: the window id the sidebar is rendering for
FLEET_SIDEBAR_TEXT                 handoff: the text the sidebar input line asked for, to fleet-sidebar-remote.sh (#1620)
FLEET_SKIP_GLOBAL_CONF             seam: fleet-lib skips the install fleet.conf (tests / isolated tools)
FLEET_SMOKE_ONBOARD_SECS           knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (fleet-login-smoke.sh)
FLEET_SMOKE_POLL_SECS              knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (fleet-login-smoke.sh)
FLEET_SMOKE_SSH_HOST               seam: where the smoke run's ssh -tt connects (127.0.0.1); --ssh-host is the operator's face (fleet-login-smoke.sh)
FLEET_SMOKE_SSH_PORT               seam: the sshd port the smoke run connects to (22); --ssh-port is the operator's face (fleet-login-smoke.sh)
FLEET_SMOKE_TIMEOUT                knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default; --timeout is the operator's face (fleet-login-smoke.sh)
FLEET_SPAWN_GUARD_SLEEP            knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (dash-enter.sh)
FLEET_SPAWN_CLAIMED                handoff: the --async tail inherits the foreground's GitHub claim, taken back on failure (#1606)
FLEET_SPAWN_TAIL                   handoff: spawn only the seed tail (used by the handoff/resume path)
FLEET_SPOT_EVACUATE_MARGIN         knob: seconds fleet-spot-evacuate.sh keeps before its deadline so a started move can finish, default 30 (#1428)
FLEET_SPOT_EVACUATE_SECS           handoff: the SPOT reclaim deadline the ccquota agent passes to fleet-spot-evacuate.sh (its CCQUOTA_FLEET_RECLAIM_SECS, 240; #1428)
FLEET_SPOT_EVACUATE_SESSIONS       seam: the fleets fleet-spot-evacuate.sh evacuates, space-separated, instead of fleet_sockets (no tmux in the selftest; #1428)
FLEET_STATUS_CACHE                 path: status-bar render cache file
FLEET_STATUS_DISK                  knob: 0 drops the disk alert (fleet-alerts.sh; the bar has no disk segment since #1616)
FLEET_STOP_CLOSE_WAIT              knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (fleet-worker-stop.sh)
FLEET_STOP_EXIT_WAIT               knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (fleet-worker-stop.sh)
FLEET_SYNC_LOGINS_DAEMON_DIR       seam: an injectable command/path for tests (fleet-sync-logins.sh)
FLEET_SYNC_LOGINS_HOMES            seam: an injectable command/path for tests (fleet-sync-logins.sh)
FLEET_SYNC_LOGINS_LAUNCHCTL        seam: an injectable command/path for tests (fleet-sync-logins.sh)
FLEET_SYNC_LOGINS_ME               seam: an injectable command/path for tests (fleet-sync-logins.sh)
FLEET_SYNC_LOGINS_PGREP            seam: an injectable command/path for tests (fleet-sync-logins.sh)
FLEET_SYNC_LOGINS_SUDO             seam: an injectable command/path for tests (fleet-sync-logins.sh)
FLEET_SYNC_LOGINS_TMP              seam: an injectable command/path for tests (fleet-sync-logins.sh)
FLEET_SYSTEMD_USER_DIR             path: systemd user unit dir override (fleet-install-apply.sh)
FLEET_TMUX_PREFIX                  handoff: the operator's tmux prefix, read by fleet-up into the keymap
FLEET_TMUX_PREFIX2                 handoff: the operator's second tmux prefix, read by fleet-up into the keymap
FLEET_TOKEN_PROBE                  seam: a fake token-probe command
FLEET_TRANSFER_BOOT_WAIT           knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (fleet-transfer.sh)
FLEET_TRANSFER_EXIT_WAIT           knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (fleet-transfer.sh)
FLEET_TRANSFER_IDLE_WAIT           knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (fleet-transfer.sh)
FLEET_TRASH_PURGE_URGENT           handoff: the cleanup daemon marks an urgent trash purge (skips the load cap)
FLEET_TRASH_SWEEP_BUDGET           knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (fleet-cleanup-daemon.sh)
FLEET_UI_QUIET                     handoff: 1 = fleet_ui_fail draws nothing — the caller re-says the failure in its own one line (dash-issue-new.sh, issue #1618)
FLEET_WEBHOOK_DEBOUNCE             knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (fleet-webhook.sh)
FLEET_WEBHOOK_EVENTS               knob: the GitHub events the webhook forwarder subscribes to (fleet-webhook.sh)
FLEET_WEBHOOK_RESCAN               knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (fleet-webhook.sh)
FLEET_WEBHOOK_STATE_DIR            path: state/log location override (fleet-webhook.sh)
FLEET_WEBHOOK_WAKE_SLACK           knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (fleet-webhook.sh)
FLEET_WEBHOOK_WAKE_TICK            knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (fleet-webhook.sh)
FLEET_WINDOW_REAP                  knob: 0 turns the close-time orphan-tree sweep off (fleet-window-reap.sh; read from the tmux server env, not a conf)
FLEET_WINDOW_REAP_EXEMPT_RE        knob: extra argv ERE the close-time sweep never reaps (fleet_orphan_trees)
FLEET_WINDOW_REAP_FG               handoff: fleet-window-reap.sh --hook re-execs itself detached with this set
FLEET_WINDOW_REAP_PASSES           knob: seconds after a close to sweep at (fleet-window-reap.sh, "2 6 20")
FLEET_WINDOW_REAP_ROOT             seam: narrow the close-time sweep to tops whose cwd is under this dir (selftests)
FLEET_WH_BACKOFF_BASE              knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (fleet-webhook.sh)
FLEET_WH_CATCHUP_MIN               knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (fleet-webhook.sh)
FLEET_WH_BACKOFF_CAP               knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (fleet-webhook.sh)
FLEET_WH_FORWARD_CMD               seam: an injectable command/path for tests (fleet-webhook.sh)
FLEET_WH_HOOKS_LIST_CMD            seam: an injectable command/path for tests (fleet-webhook.sh)
FLEET_WH_HOOK_DEL_CMD              seam: an injectable command/path for tests (fleet-webhook.sh)
FLEET_WH_HOOK_HOST                 seam: the relay host a forwarder hook is recognised by (fleet-webhook.sh)
FLEET_WH_NOW_FILE                  seam: a fixed clock for the webhook backoff
FLEET_WH_SLEEP_CMD                 seam: an injectable command/path for tests (fleet-webhook.sh)
FLEET_WORKER_PROMPT_FILE           alias: retired twin of FLEET_WORKER_PROMPT="@<path>" (#1101) — still read, wins when set
FLEET_WORKTREE_SETUP_LOG           path: state/log location override (fleet-lib.sh)
FLEET_X                            doc: the placeholder name in a comment, not a key
FLEET_GH_FAKE_LIMIT                seam: inject a GitHub rate limit per bucket for tests, never touches the account (fleet-gh-lib.sh, #1042)
FLEET_GH_LIMIT_HOLD_SECS           knob: internal pacing/limit, safe in-code default (fleet-gh-lib.sh)
FLEET_GH_LOG                       path: state/log location override (fleet-gh-lib.sh)
FLEET_GH_LEADER_STALE              knob: internal timeout, seconds a leader heartbeat stays live (3 collector ticks; fleet-gh-lib.sh, #1271)
FLEET_GH_SHARED_DIR                path: machine-wide dir the logins of one token share (fleet-gh-lib.sh, #1271)
FLEET_GH_SHARE_ID                  seam: this login's name in the leader election, lets one test user play two logins (fleet-gh-lib.sh, #1271)
FLEET_GH_WRITE_BACKOFF             knob: internal pacing, secondary-limit backoff base without Retry-After (fleet-gh-lib.sh write queue, #1264)
FLEET_GH_WRITE_GAP                 knob: internal pacing, min seconds between write starts per token (fleet-gh-lib.sh write queue, #1264)
FLEET_GH_WRITE_LOCK_WAIT           knob: internal timeout, longest a writer queues before writing unqueued (fleet-gh-lib.sh, #1264)
FLEET_GH_WH_MAX_AGE                knob: longest an event-quiet prmap still serves while the webhook is live (fleet-gh.sh, 300, #1272)
FLEET_STATE_DIR                    path: state/log location override — the shared gh-limit marker dir (fleet-gh-lib.sh)
FLEET_SHOW_OUT                     test seam: where fleet-show-send.py writes instead of /dev/tty (fleet-show-selftest.sh, #1367)
FLEET_OPEN_SECRET_FILE             seam: the shared secret's path (fleet-open-selftest.sh, #1379)
FLEET_OPEN_URL_BIN                 seam: the fallback opener instead of bin/open-url.sh (fleet-open-selftest.sh, #1379)
FLEET_LOOP_BACKFILL_BYTES          knob: internal budget, transcript tail bytes the Stop hook replays to backfill a pre-hook @loop (fleet_stop_wait, 262144, #1370)
FLEET_WAIT_REEVAL                  knob: 0 turns off the idle-window re-ask of done ↔ looping + @claude_wait (fleet-wait-reeval.sh, on, #1376)
FLEET_HUB_CACHE_SECS               knob: internal budget, seconds the hub worker cache (control/hub-workers.tsv) stays fresh for fleet_worker_locate (30, #1420)
FLEET_HUB_STATUS_CMD               seam: command printing `<worker_id>\t<node>` that refreshes the hub worker cache; the ccquota agent now writes the cache itself (#1421); kept for a hub reached some other way (fleet_worker_locate, #1420)
FLEET_HUB_SESSIONS_CMD             seam: command printing the hub's fleet_sessions JSON instead of GET $CCQUOTA_HUB_URL/v1/fleet/fleet_sessions (fleet-hub-sessions.sh, #1423)
FLEET_HUB_SESSIONS_EVERY           knob: internal pacing, seconds between the remote-sessions refreshes (fleet-hub-sessions.sh, 10, #1423)
FLEET_HUB_SESSIONS_WATCHED_EVERY   knob: internal pacing, seconds between the refreshes while a client is attached to any session of this fleet — the loop sends If-None-Match so an unchanged hub answers 304 (fleet-hub-sessions.sh, 2, #1481)
FLEET_HUB_SESSIONS_WAIT            knob: internal pacing, seconds the hub may hold a watched fleet_sessions ask (long poll) until a heartbeat moves its ETag — capped at 25, under an ingress's 60 s idle timeout (fleet-hub-sessions.sh, 25, #1526)
FLEET_HUB_SESSIONS_LONGPOLL        knob: 0 = the watched loop never sends `wait` and keeps its fixed 2 s cadence (fleet-hub-sessions.sh, 1, #1526)
FLEET_HUB_SESSIONS_STATUS_STALE    knob: seconds of hub_ok age past which `fleet-hub-sessions.sh --status` (fleet-doctor's hub-sessions row) reports the refresh stalled (fleet-hub-sessions.sh, 60, #1596)
FLEET_HUB_SESSIONS_LOOP_SECS       knob: internal budget, how long one detached refresh loop lives before the next collector tick restarts it (70, #1423)
FLEET_HUB_SESSIONS_STALE           knob: internal budget, seconds of hub silence (global/hub_ok, else the cache's #ts) after which the dash reads every remote row as 失联, the bar `入口 ○`, and a remote-row action refuses — fleet_status_hub_lost in fleet-status-lib.sh (60, #1423 #1483)
FLEET_HUB_NODE_TIMEOUT             knob: internal budget, seconds the shell's loop gives ONE machine to answer `fleet-remote-view.sh sessions` over its ssh control connection while the hub is silent — client mode only, node_refresh in fleet-hub-sessions.sh (8, #1488)
FLEET_REMOTE_BIN                   knob: the fleet's bin/ on the other machine for a proxy window, default .claude/fleet/bin (fleet-remote-view.sh, #1424)
FLEET_REMOTE_VIA_HUB               knob: 0 = a proxy window never falls back to the hub relay (fleet-remote-view.sh, #1424)
FLEET_REMOTE_SSH_CMD               seam: the ssh program a proxy window runs (fleet-remote-view-selftest.sh)
FLEET_REMOTE_OPENER                seam: what re-issues a remote fleet-open request (fleet-remote-view-selftest.sh)
FLEET_HUB_URL                      handoff: the hub URL `fleet connect` (fleet-connect.py) reads; fleet-remote-view.sh only checks it is set before trying the relay (#1424)
FLEET_HUB_SESSIONS_CLIENT          handoff: the shell's pseudo-fleet name — fleet-hub-sessions.sh serves that one name, every row remote, no control adapter (fleet-shell.sh, #1484)
FLEET_SHELL                        handoff: 1 in the shell's tmux server environment — fleet-remote-view.sh open starts `run --shell`, fleet-sidebar.sh runs without a fleet conf; 0 in a person's environment keeps `fleet` on the direct way in (bin/fleet, fleet-shell.sh, #1484)
FLEET_SHELL_SESSION                knob: the shell's tmux session + socket label (fleet-shell.sh, fleet-shell, #1484)
FLEET_SHELL_CACHE                  path: the shell's own cache root — its bin/ mirror, tmux.conf and $TMPDIR (fleet-shell.sh, ~/.cache/claude-fleet/shell, #1484)
FLEET_SHELL_PREFIX                 knob: the shell's tmux prefix (fleet-shell.sh, C-b, #1484)
FLEET_SHELL_WIDTH                  knob: the shell's list width (fleet-shell.sh → FLEET_SIDEBAR_WIDTH, 30, #1484)
FLEET_SHELL_NO_ATTACH              seam: 1 = start the shell's server and print its session instead of attaching, so bin/fleet picks the shell with no terminal (fleet-shell-selftest.sh)
FLEET_SHELL_WARM                   knob: 0 = no warm ssh masters in the shell (fleet-shell.sh warm, on by default, #1631)
FLEET_SHELL_WARM_MAX               knob: at most this many machines kept warm, busiest first (fleet-shell.sh warm, 4, #1631)
FLEET_SHELL_WARM_EVERY             knob: seconds between warm-loop ticks (fleet-shell.sh warm, 5, #1631)
FLEET_SHELL_WARM_CONNECT           seam: the command that opens a warm master instead of fleet-connect.py (fleet-shell-warm-selftest.sh, #1631)
FLEET_CONNECT_ROUTE_FILE           handoff: fleet-remote-view.sh → fleet-connect.py, where the chosen route is written for the pane (#1628)
FLEET_CONNECT_RETEST               handoff: fleet-remote-view.sh → fleet-connect.py, 1 = re-measure every route on a reconnect (#1628)
FLEET_CONNECT_PROBE_CMD            seam: the direct probe the shell's upgrader runs (fleet-fallback-selftest.sh)
FLEET_CONNECT_UPGRADE_SECS         knob: on the hub relay, seconds between direct probes (15, #1628)
FLEET_REMOTE_IDLE_SECS             knob: seconds without a key before the upgrader switches lines (2, #1628)
FLEET_HUB_SESSIONS_USER            knob: whose sessions on the other machines the dash shows (os_user; default `id -un`, `*` = every login the hub shows; #1423)
FLEET_CERT                         handoff: the connection-certificate key pair a sidebar / `fleet connect` signs with — the key; `<key>-cert.pub` beside it (default ~/.ssh/fleet-cert, what `fleet login` wrote; fleet-hub-sessions.sh, fleet-connect.py, #1475)
FLEET_HUB_LEASE_CMD                seam: the hub issue-lease command (default `ccquota lease`), run as `<cmd> acquire|release [--force] <repo> <issue> <worker_id>` (fleet_hub_lease, #1422)
FLEET_HUB_RETAIN_SECS              knob: internal budget, seconds a hub worker map may age before remote children stop holding their parent (600, #1421)
FLEET_HUB_CURL                     seam: the transport fleet-node-maintenance.sh calls the hub with (default `curl`; the selftest's fake records argv + body; #1427)
FLEET_HUB_TIMEOUT                  knob: seconds fleet-node-maintenance.sh waits on one hub call (curl --max-time), default 15 (#1427)
FLEET_HUB_PLACE_CMD                seam: the hub placement command (default `ccquota place`), run as `<cmd> --node <n> [--origin-wid <w>] [--agent <a>] <repo> <issue> <worker_id>` (fleet_hub_place, #1425)
FLEET_HUB_MOVE_CMD                 seam: the hub session-move command (default `ccquota move`), run as `<cmd> plan|send [<flag>…] <repo> <worker_id>` (fleet_hub_move, #1426)
FLEET_HUB_WRITE_CMD                seam: command run as `<cmd> <tool> <args_json>` in place of the hub write doors (viewer-token POST /v1/fleet/<tool>, device-signed POST /v1/fleet/write) — the sidebar selftest records what the remote-row menu writes (fleet-hub-write.sh, #1487)
FLEET_HUB_NODE_SUDO                seam: the privilege prefix `fleet-hub-node.sh env --write` reads a root-owned agent plist with (default `sudo -n`; empty = none) (#1491)
FLEET_HUB_NODE_DAEMON_DIR          seam: where `fleet-hub-node.sh env --write` looks for the system LaunchDaemon com.ccquota.agent.<login>.plist (default /Library/LaunchDaemons) (#1491)
FLEET_JOIN_SUDO                    seam: the privilege prefix fleet-node-join.sh uses for package installs / system units (default `sudo -n`; empty = none) (#1418)
FLEET_JOIN_OS                      seam: overrides `uname -s` in fleet-node-join.sh (darwin|linux) (#1418)
FLEET_JOIN_ARCH                    seam: overrides `uname -m` in fleet-node-join.sh (#1418)
FLEET_JOIN_POLL                    seam: seconds between fleet-node-join.sh's /v1/node/self polls (default 3) (#1418)
FLEET_NODE_JOIN_ARGS               seam: extra fleet-node-join.sh options `fleet node join` passes through (fleet-node-selftest: --no-deps --service detached …) (#1627)
FLEET_HUB_NODES_CMD                seam: command printing the hub's /v1/nodes JSON instead of a GET (fleet-hub-sessions.sh refresh_summaries, #1482)
FLEET_HUB_LIMITS_CMD               seam: command printing the hub's /v1/limits?account=all JSON instead of a GET (fleet-hub-sessions.sh refresh_summaries, #1482)
FLEET_STATUS_G                     path: the status bar's cache dir (global/, where hub_nodes / hub_limits / remote_<sess> live) — a selftest sandbox (fleet-status-lib.sh, #1482)
FLEET_HUB_SUMMARY_EVERY            knob: seconds between the status-bar summaries (/v1/nodes + /v1/limits) a refresh round fetches, 0 = every round (fleet-hub-sessions.sh, 10, #1482)
FLEET_DOCTOR_AGENT_TARGET          seam: the target the doctor's `agent` line compares against instead of `stable` (fleet-doctor.sh → fleet-node-upgrade.sh --status, #1525)
FLEET_NODE_UPGRADE_DAEMON_DIR      seam: where fleet-node-upgrade.sh finds the com.ccquota.agent.<login>.plist LaunchDaemons (default /Library/LaunchDaemons) (#1525)
FLEET_NODE_UPGRADE_AGENT_DIR       seam: where fleet-node-upgrade.sh finds this login's com.ccquota.agent.plist LaunchAgent (default ~/Library/LaunchAgents) (#1525)
FLEET_NODE_UPGRADE_PS              seam: command printing `uid pid path` rows instead of ps (fleet-node-upgrade.sh, #1525)
FLEET_NODE_UPGRADE_UIDS            seam: "login=uid …" consulted before `id -u` (fleet-node-upgrade.sh, #1525)
FLEET_NODE_UPGRADE_SUDO            seam: the privilege prefix for install / kickstart (default `sudo -n`; empty = none) (fleet-node-upgrade.sh, #1525)
FLEET_NODE_UPGRADE_LAUNCHCTL       seam: the launchctl binary (fleet-node-upgrade.sh, #1525)
FLEET_NODE_UPGRADE_NODES_CMD       seam: command printing the hub's /v1/nodes JSON instead of a GET (fleet-node-upgrade.sh, #1525)
FLEET_NODE_UPGRADE_HOSTNAME        seam: overrides `hostname -s` — which /v1/nodes rows are this machine's (fleet-node-upgrade.sh, #1525)
FLEET_NODE_UPGRADE_OS              seam: overrides `uname -s` (fleet-node-upgrade.sh is launchd-only, #1525)
FLEET_NODE_UPGRADE_POLL            seam: seconds between post-restart hub polls (default 2) (fleet-node-upgrade.sh, #1525)
FLEET_PEER_CERT                    escape hatch: 0 = never ask the hub for a machine-to-machine certificate, plain ssh (fleet-peer-cert.sh, #1626)
FLEET_PEER_CERT_SECS               seam: life asked for a peer certificate (default 300; the hub caps it at 300) (fleet-peer-cert.sh, #1626)
FLEET_PEER_CERT_MARGIN             knob: seconds before expiry a cached peer certificate stops being reused (fleet-peer-cert.sh, 30, #1631)
FLEET_PEER_CERT_CONNECT_SECS       seam: connect bound for the peer-cert request — a down hub is refused inside 1 s (default 0.8) (fleet-peer-cert.sh, #1630)
FLEET_WORKER_RECORDS               escape hatch: 0 = never hand a reaped worker's evidence/history to the hub nor read others' back (fleet-worker-records.sh, #1609)
FLEET_WORKER_RECORDS_IMG_MAX       seam: image size in bytes above which push shrinks it with sips (default 614400) (fleet-worker-records.sh, #1609)
FLEET_PEER_KEY                     path: the peer key the hub signs (default ~/.ssh/fleet-peer) (fleet-peer-cert.sh, #1626)
